WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.463
Here's what the shared
client already does.

2
00:00:02.463 --> 00:00:07.112
It builds SailPoint's base URL from
the tenant name, or takes one you set.

3
00:00:07.112 --> 00:00:10.502
It gets a token from a vault
or by client credentials;

4
00:00:10.502 --> 00:00:13.262
a personal access token
works the same way.

5
00:00:13.262 --> 00:00:16.351
Search pages with
search-after, sorted on the ID,

6
00:00:16.351 --> 00:00:20.312
which is how SailPoint says to
get past ten thousand results.

7
00:00:20.312 --> 00:00:25.099
Account lists page two hundred
fifty at a time, the API's maximum.

8
00:00:25.099 --> 00:00:29.050
Graph uses a certificate first,
from the cloud's own authority.

9
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:31.676
And because Search has no accounts index,

10
00:00:31.676 --> 00:00:34.750
one account is re-read
through the Accounts API.
